    "body": "fix on issue/1305-posed-band-cylinder · PR #1307 · pinned by `verify::posed_steel::tests::{a_holder_just_over_a_clamp_is_clear_at_a_small_real_lean, the_holder_is_struck_once_its_rim_really_reaches_the_clamp, the_verdict_turns_once_and_at_the_true_touching_lean, a_fixed_clamp_under_the_stood_up_holder_is_clear_at_any_lean, steel_at_any_point_of_the_true_leaning_band_is_struck, a_non_finite_band_or_box_is_never_proven_clear}` and `crates/sim/tests/posed_band_cylinder.rs` · merges when reviewed\n\nNote: `main` has neither #938 (PR #973, open) nor #1303 (open, no branch pushed), so this is built on upstream/main alone. In the path frame law (c2)'s own column enclosure (`stack_span::band_struck`, #1303) still convicts the evidence case at 0.01 degrees through `bands_vs_fixtures`; the posed sweep's own verdict is now clear there (pinned at `posed_hits`) and end to end where the sweep alone decides (fixed steel under a rotary). The \"0.01 degrees is not convicted\" half of Done-means holds end to end only once #1303 merges too.\n",
